BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (information, inode areas, replicated critical metadata and data blocks. The original design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (explicitly places related inodes and blocks close to one another to reduce seeks on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (rotating media.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Inodes store mode, ownership, timestamps, link count, size and a direct/indirect block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (addressing scheme. Large files require indirect pointer blocks. Fragments allow the final) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (portion of a small file to consume less than a full block. The disk's real format variant,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (byte order and filesystem parameters determine exact field offsets; an ext2 inode cannot be) Tj ET
