BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (Cylinder groups are the primary allocation unit, with policies spreading directories and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (clustering the data of individual files. A free-space bitmap and summary information help) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (the allocator find blocks and fragments. Full block allocation favours performance, while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (fragment allocation limits tail waste. Contemporary media no longer have the original seek) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (assumptions, but format-level structures remain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Directories contain name-to-inode records. Hard links reference the same inode and share) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (data; file removal changes link counts and allocator state. Directories must be scanned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (with explicit record-length and name-length bounds. The root inode and directory hierarchy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (must be consistent with group allocation metadata.) Tj ET
