BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (The principal breakthrough was allocation locality, larger transfer units and block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (fragments rather than a novel journal. The implementation balanced sequential throughput) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (and space efficiency by selecting block and fragment sizes, spreading inodes and localising) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (access. Original policies assume properties of rotating magnetic media.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 599.0 Tm (UFS1 inode, timestamp and capacity widths constrained later deployments. UFS2 was designed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (because incremental expansion of UFS1 was not sufficient for multi-terabyte systems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (Current FreeBSD support may differ from historical BSD, and physical layout details vary by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (implementation version.) Tj ET
